+# WP-S contracts v1 — 2026-11-11
+
+Source: PLAN amendment and critic findings 1–12 at base `de30ccfa5f999e37b14fcd5ee9dbf4566e373154`.
+These contracts freeze implementation seams for B/C/D. Endpoints below are contracts, not implemented routes.
+InternalDbContext remains authoritative. StoreDbContext and the public simulator remain separate.
+
+## WP-B: publication and SSE
+
+`EventOutbox`: EventId (unique GUID), Type, SchemaVersion, ResourceId, OriginalBranchId,
+OccurredAt, PayloadJson, nullable PublicationPosition (bigint), PublisherState (pending/published).
+EventId identifies a semantic change; position identifies publication order. They are never interchangeable.
+Unique (Type, ResourceId) uses the change ID: sale ID for sale.paid, reversal ID for refunds,
+movement/receipt/adjustment ID for stock, till ID for open/close. Do not use an item ID for repeat changes.
+Payload v1 is `{}`: an invalidation, never a receipt, customer, amount, or contact snapshot.
+Branchless events are stored but denied by the staff stream. Do not infer a branch later.
+
+The reference producer is cash.sale, inside its existing runner callback after payment SaveChanges.
+Its deterministic EventId is SaleId. Exceptions/rejections roll back with the action/savepoint.
+Same-key replay bypasses the callback. No network delivery occurs inside the financial transaction.
+No runner refactor is needed: existing rollback plus ChangeTracker.Clear already covers the new tracked row.
+Other producers belong to B and must distinguish a new semantic change from a successful no-op.
+
+Use `InternalOutboxWriter.AssignPublicationPositions` with a fresh context after source commits.
+All publisher instances acquire transaction-owned SQL lock `SaviaInternal:outbox-publisher:v1`.
+Under that lock, read MAX published position, scan up to 100 pending rows, assign increasing positions,
+save and commit atomically. SQL ReadCommitted exposes only committed source rows; it may wait on writers.
+A source committing late remains pending and receives a later position on the next scan.
+OccurredAt/GUID sort selects a batch, never defines a replay checkpoint. No READPAST over allocated positions.
+Retry after uncertain commit reloads durable state; assigned positions never change.
+Do not delete the row holding the highest published position. Retention must preserve this high-water sentinel,
+even if its event expires from replay. Removing all published rows would reuse positions and violates this contract.
+Only this publisher may assign positions; no direct producer assignment or sequence/identity default.
+SSE reads committed rows with assigned positions, not only rows newly marked published.
+
+GET `/internal/api/events`; cookie authentication; no URL credentials.
+Cursor: `v1:<positive decimal bigint>` in Last-Event-ID and SSE id. Parse as Int64 on server and string in JS.
+No cursor means authorized refresh plus current high-water checkpoint before consuming subsequent invalidations.
+Transport is at least once. UI deduplicates positions/event IDs and refetches authoritative authorized projections.
+No financial delta application. Reconnect must subscribe to the durable log through the same high-water handoff.
+Retain replay for 7 days; max 100 rows/page, 256 buffered frames/client, 4 streams/session, 100 streams/host.
+Disconnect slow clients on overflow. Invalid/unknown/future/expired cursors get `reset` with no private data;
+client clears its checkpoint, refreshes authorized state, then reconnects. Never silently skip a range.
+The retained sentinel is not replayable after expiry. B owns cleanup and a retention-floor test.
+
+| Topic | Owner | Manager | Cashier | Inventory | Anonymous |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| sale.paid, sale.refunded, sale.returned, sale.cancelled | Any active branch | Current branch | Current branch, own till/resource only | Deny | Deny |
+| stock.changed, stock.received | Any active branch | Current branch | Current branch | Current branch | Deny |
+| till.opened, till.closed | Any active branch | Current branch | Current branch, own till only | Deny | Deny |
+| customer.changed | Deny (use authorized CRM read) | Deny | Deny | Deny | Deny |
+| Unknown or branchless topic | Deny | Deny | Deny | Deny | Deny |
+
+For every batch, resolve resource custody from server state and compare original event branch to current membership.
+Manager cannot opt into another branch. Owner global is explicit, never an inferred default for other roles.
+Revalidate persisted session, security version, staff enabled/role, active branch and resource before each batch
+and at idle intervals ≤1 second. On storage error or revocation, close without sending another batch.
+Revocation bound: ≤1 second after persisted revocation becomes observable; already-sent bytes cannot be recalled.
+Browser closes on logout/session epoch change and ignores stale callbacks. B tests busy and idle streams,
+Owner recovery, reassignment, expiry, two clients, two branches, commit inversion and crash recovery.
+
+## WP-C: staff customer admission
+
+Policy name: `internal.customer-admission`. Roles Owner, Manager, Cashier; deny Inventory/anonymous/revoked sessions.
+Search is global across branches, intentionally limited to DTO `{id,name,email,phone}` for active customers.
+Never expose purchases, spend, notes, address, consent history, suppliers, or staff. No bulk listing or total count.
+GET `/internal/api/customers/search?kind=email|name&mode=exact|prefix&q=...&take=...`.
+Email uses canonical normalization below. Name uses trimmed NFC. Exact email or name prefix ≥3 characters;
+maximum q length 254, take default 10/max 20, no offset, wildcards or empty query.
+Exact name is permitted with ≥3 characters. Match prefixes as escaped literals. 30 searches/min/session, 300/host;
+limiter returns 429/Retry-After. Bound concurrency and never trust forwarded IP without configured proxies.
+
+POST `/internal/api/customers`: `{name,email,phone?,choice:"create-new"|"choose-existing",existingId?}`.
+Require same-session CSRF and actor-bound idempotency. Normal registration requires nonempty validated name/email.
+Search exact normalized email first; show minimal matches and require an explicit selection or explicit create-new.
+Never automatically merge. Choosing requires an active customer returned under the same authorization rules;
+recheck at write time. Optional customer on sale stays optional. Existing Owner directory authority stays unchanged.
+New cash admission command scope must be added explicitly by C; the current runner does not yet grant it.
+Responses use the minimal DTO only; avoid adding new immutable PII receipts (see erasure gate).
+
+Canonical email: Trim → NFC → ToLowerInvariant. Preserve plus tags and dots; never infer provider aliases.
+Parties.NormalizedEmail has a non-unique binary index. Existing shared/null/supplier contacts remain legal.
+The Email setter maintains normalized values for new application writes. Existing migration rows remain NULL:
+SQL cannot reproduce .NET NFC safely. C owns an explicit bounded application backfill before indexed search activation,
+with old contact bytes preserved and historical duplicates reported to Owner, never merged.
+Do not treat NULL normalization as absence of a legacy match. Until backfill completes, admission/search stays gated.
+WebsiteAccounts has a separate unique binary NormalizedEmail index, linked to Party with Restrict deletion.
+C/D normalize with InternalCustomerEmail before insert and use SQL uniqueness as the final concurrency barrier.
+An anonymous claim never attaches an account to a preexisting Party by email alone.
+Account email remains reserved after disable/withdrawal, preventing retries from silently restoring consent.
+
+## WP-D: public catalog and signup
+
+GET `/api/catalog`: allowlist `{items:[{id,sku,name,unitPriceMinor,currency,available}],asOf}`.
+Only active items explicitly included in an Owner-approved publication map. Empty map publishes zero items.
+Map placeholder (configuration, not inferred): public product/variant ID → InternalItemId + allowed active LocationIds.
+D owns the map implementation and an approval artifact; no historical website ID matching by guess.
+Availability = sum(OnHand - Reserved) over mapped active locations only. Missing balance is zero.
+Include exception allocation effects only through authoritative balances; never invent reservations absent from Internal.
+No costs, internal location/branch names, customers, staff, supplier, till, ledger or operation data.
+Money uses integer minor units plus explicit ISO currency; no conversion. Reject mixed-currency aggregation.
+Page size max 100; bounded polling ≤5 seconds, cache timestamp/age, stale/offline state visibly identified.
+Public catalog does not consume the private staff SSE endpoint. Latency/Web Vitals require real browser proof in D.
+
+POST `/api/customer-signups`: `{name,email,phone?,consent:{purpose,policyVersion,accepted}}` only.
+Reject unknown fields and client-supplied IDs, roles, branch, staff actor, verification or internal flags.
+Purpose allowlist starts with `customer-registration`; marketing requires its own explicit approved policy and opt-in.
+Server records time, anonymous actor type, source `website`; StaffActorId stays null.
+Account state is unverified until a separate proof of ownership flow is approved and implemented.
+Use a dedicated anonymous service, never a fabricated staff session or InternalCommandRunner bypass.
+One SQL transaction inserts normalized unique account + new Party + explicit consent. On uniqueness race, rollback
+and return the same generic result; do not overwrite contact, attach to a legacy Party, or regrant withdrawn consent.
+All syntactically valid new/existing/inactive/withdrawn requests return 202 `{"status":"received"}`.
+Invalid bodies return generic 400; max body 4 KiB, name 200/email 254/phone 32.
+Rate limits: 5/min/client, 100/min/host, max 4 concurrent admissions, bounded limiter state and 429/Retry-After.
+No staff cookies/CSRF authority on this endpoint; enforce configured origin and proxy trust explicitly.
+Replayed signup must not change consent or restore disabled/anonymized records. D tests concurrent C/D writes.
+
+## Consent, anonymization and retained replay copies
+
+No existing Party gets consent automatically. No consent row means unknown/not granted.
+Consent records purpose, policy version, server timestamp, actor type/source, nullable real staff actor and withdrawal.
+Withdrawal must be one-way at the service layer and must not be reset by retries; C/D own this service enforcement.
+This schema alone does not enforce all lifecycle transitions or provide an anonymization endpoint.
+
+Anonymization primitive design: preserve Party.Id as an inactive tombstone with neutral name, clear Email,
+NormalizedEmail and Phone, disable website admission and withdraw consent. Never delete sale/customer FKs,
+payments, refunds, cash close totals or stock/item snapshots. This is accounting pseudonymization.
+The current append-only Operations.ResultJson contains historical InternalPartyView name/email/phone.
+Party-only anonymization leaves those copies accessible through original-key replay. The focused retained-copy test
+records this exact limitation. The fingerprint is also retained as an irreversible request hash, not raw request text.
+Retention reason today: immutable replay/audit contract and GuardAudit; no approved selective erasure implementation exists.
+Do not advertise erasure or activate an anonymization endpoint while replay still returns these contacts.
+Required follow-on by primary/C: narrow audited operation-erasure overlay or PII-free receipt plus current projection,
+applied to both command replay and recovery GET, including old operation JSON. Do not relax GuardAudit globally.
+WebsiteAccounts.NormalizedEmail also remains identifying data; reserve a keyed tombstone rather than raw email
+only after an approved lookup/retention design. No keys or salts belong in this repository.
+Existing exports, browser caches, logs, backups and legal retention are UNKNOWN; Owner must inventory them.
+Outbox v1 adds no contact payload. Resource GUID linkage remains pseudonymous accounting data.
+
