+## Mechanism and source seam
+
+Publication positions are assigned after source commit by a SQL-lock-serialized publisher, not a precommit sequence.
+Every publisher transaction takes `SaviaInternal:outbox-publisher:v1`, reads committed pending rows and persists
+new positions atomically. A late committed row gets a higher position in a later batch. Existing positions survive retries.
+MAX requires retaining the highest published row forever as a high-water sentinel; CONTRACTS makes this mandatory.
+The expired sentinel is excluded from replay by B. No network runs inside source or assignment transactions.
+This is a source-level safety argument; concurrency SQL proof remains pending.
+
+The reference writer runs in cash.sale after the payment SaveChanges and inside the existing runner callback.
+EventId and ResourceId equal SaleId. The existing savepoint and tracker cleanup need no runner modification.
+Same-key replay returns before the callback. Exceptional sales follow the same paid path without requiring a stock movement.
+No other producers were added. Frozen payload is `{}`; no receipt or contact fields are broadcast.
